	<li><a name="n2" id="n2"></a>Refers to total  participation rate for those age 16 and older; estimates are as of October 2017. Source: Bureau of Labor Statistics, <a href="http://www.bls.gov/opub/mlr/2017/article/projections-overview-and-highlights-2016-26.htm">www.bls.gov/opub/mlr/2017/article/projections-overview-and-highlights-2016-26.htm</a>.</li>
	
	<li><a name="n3" id="n3"></a>Wilshire 5000 Price Index (Full Capitalization)/GDP, as of Sept. 29, 2017. Sources: Dow Jones and Bureau of Economic Analysis.</li>
	
	<li><a name="n4" id="n4"></a>According to the monthly average of daily close of the CBOE Market Volatility Index New Methodology (VIX), October 2017 had the lowest levels on record.</li>
	
	<li><a name="n5" id="n5"></a>As of Nov. 16, 2017. Source: LPL Financial Research, published on Oct. 22, 2017, <a href="https://lplresearch.com/2017/10/22/here-it-comes-the-longest-streak-ever-without-a-3-correction/">https://lplresearch.com/2017/10/22/here-it-comes-the-longest-streak-ever-without-a-3-correction/</a>.</li>
	
	<li><a name="n6" id="n6"></a>Refers to nonfinancial corporate debt as a percent of GDP as of second quarter 2017. Sources: Federal Reserve Board and Bureau of Economic Analysis.</li>
	
	<li><a name="n7" id="n7"></a>U.S. Treasury and Bureau of Economic Analysis, as of third quarter 2017.</li>
	
	<li><a name="n8" id="n8"></a>&ldquo;The 2017 Annual Report of the Board of Trustees of the Federal Old-Age and Survivors Insurance and Federal Disability Insurance Trust Funds,&rdquo; U.S. Social Security Administration, July 13, 2017; &ldquo;The 2017 Annual Report of the Boards of Trustees of the Federal Hospital Insurance and Federal Supplementary Medical Insurance Trust Funds,&rdquo; Centers for Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services, July 13, 2017.</li>
	
	<li><a name="n9" id="n9"></a>2017 levels are averages from January&ndash;October 2017. 2007 levels are averages from January&ndash;December 2007. Trading volume refers to average dollar volume. Sources: NYSE; World Federation of Exchanges; Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas calculations.</li>
	
	<li><a name="n10" id="n10"></a>As of Oct. 31, 2017. Source: NYSE.</li>
	
	<li><a name="n11" id="n11"></a>&ldquo;The Condition of Education 2017 (NCES 2017-144),&rdquo; Undergraduate Retention and Graduation Rates, U.S. Department of Education, National Center for Education Statistics, 2017.</li>
